.TH EMACSVOX 1 "September 2026" "Emacsvox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
emacsvox \- start the Emacsvox audio desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emacsvox
.RI [ launcher-options ]
.RB [ -- ]
.RI [ emacs-arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts GNU Emacs with Emacsvox, using an isolated configuration.
Requires Emacs 30.2 or newer and local Omnivox or a configured remote
workstation speech service. Personal and site startup files are not loaded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --diagnose
Report the selected Emacs, speech server and installation paths without audio.
.TP
.B --check
Run the audible speech-server check. Confirm both tone and speech.
.TP
.B --remote
Use workstation speech through an existing SSH reverse forward.
No local speech engine is required. Combine with --diagnose or --check.
.TP
.B --help
Display launcher usage and environment options.
.TP
.B --
Pass subsequent options directly to Emacs. Use -nw for a local terminal session.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EMACS
Select a supported Emacs executable.
.TP
.B OMNIVOX_PROGRAM
Absolute path to the Omnivox executable, overriding the per-user selection.
.TP
.B EMACSVOX_DIR
Override the installed Emacsvox tree, for example to test a source checkout.
.TP
.B EMACSVOX_REMOTE_HOST, EMACSVOX_REMOTE_PORT, EMACSVOX_REMOTE_TOKEN_FILE
Remote loopback endpoint and private authentication token file.
See --help and the manual for defaults and tunnel preparation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/emacsvox
Lisp sources, sounds, server launcher and offline manuals.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/emacsvox/README.Debian
Package installation, optional dependencies and configuration guidance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR emacs (1)
.PP
The full manual is /usr/share/emacsvox/info/emacsvox.info.
